# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the Swift evaluation window (tp4/swift; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/swift and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-swift-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint with its own converted-weight directory (never the base's); a job without them is the base,
# byte for byte what production serves.
# SW1 (STOP): the SMOKE of Swift on the approved ship-4 profile, on the warm cache W0 built. warmup; coding (a Python rewrite of a shell script); prefill_ladder_solo (the
# solo prefill at about 4k, 32k, 128k and 254k tokens: the long-context rung is the nearest this stack has to a needle test, and the smoke check reads its text for
# garbage); concurrent8_steady (eight users, the octo rounds); coding_set (twenty self-checking Python problems, thinking on, greedy as the request contract forces, eight
# at a time, 12,288 tokens at most each; the answers are saved whole as coding-set-<profile>.json in the results). CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py
# --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=...
# weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: created|found" line, and the worker's "[QWEN-C2]
# checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. READ: c2_smoke_check clean (no garbage text, no stall, the steady rule), the warm
# "ready=1 after N s" recorded (against W0's cold one). The coding set is READ ON A CPU HOST with SB1's: python3 scripts/ci/swift_coding_report.py --run base=<SB1
# coding-set-<profile>.json> --run swift=<this job's coding-set-<profile>.json> (it runs model-written code: a disposable host only). TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1,
# scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A
# rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the checkpoint. Duration (estimate): 70 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,prefill_ladder_solo,concurrent8_steady,coding_set
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=110
